Notebook[{
Cell["Hypergraph", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"3bc39a95-55ae-a243-9a52-311c03bd0908"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"edge1", ",", " ", "edge2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cf162821-a4fd-fe40-b62a-26b508e7cf1a"],
 " ",
 "builds a hypergraph from a list of Edge objects; its vertex set is the \
union of the vertices of those edges."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"9b63f26c-3423-f74f-88a4-2a25b20be7dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"v1", ",", " ", "v2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", "...", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "...", "}"}], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "35810aa1-1b17-5b44-a9b1-fa66f4417a99"],
 " ",
 "builds a hypergraph on an explicit vertex list, with edges given as lists \
of vertex identifiers, directed and unlabelled by default."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"8c058eb9-df9f-7248-9f2e-78ceb0923d14"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"v1", ",", " ", "v2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f1b86204-0cac-cf4f-b94d-b117eb8b322a"],
 " ",
 "builds an edgeless hypergraph on the given vertices."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"9af947ee-63cb-0847-b569-bb6d9d5fba80"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"7910e1fa-b495-5242-935e-b02b9a4653bd"],

Cell["\<\
A Hypergraph is a multiset of edges: the order of the edges carries no \
information, and a repeated edge counts once for each occurrence.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9c97a1f4-81f1-4042-9e66-1e1836e76ba9"],

Cell["\<\
The vertex list and the edge list are both put into a canonical order when \
the hypergraph is built, so two ways of writing the same hypergraph produce \
literally the same expression and may be compared with ===.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6149588a-7c07-e74f-a4da-d5bb6e1d7531"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices occurring only inside edges are absorbed into the vertex set.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"91a5863b-469b-a34d-8dc6-520d5760b730"],

Cell["\<\
A label attached to any occurrence of a vertex propagates to every other \
occurrence of that identifier. If two occurrences disagree, the explicit \
vertex list wins and the message Hypergraph::vlbl is produced.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b825868b-0709-8e4f-94d1-efa7a1fc86d9"],

Cell["\<\
A Hypergraph displays as a drawing of itself, the way a Graph does; see \
HypergraphPlot. Feeding the displayed output back to the kernel recovers the \
object. A hypergraph too large to draw usefully displays as a summary box \
instead; see HypergraphLargeQ.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"16bfe992-d4d1-c942-b172-9e9ad2447482"],

Cell["\<\
VertexList, EdgeList, VertexCount and EdgeCount work directly on a \
Hypergraph. They are protected System` symbols, extended here with UpValues \
rather than redefined.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cf91084f-37bd-cc46-bde8-f489d4b6f8f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Properties are read as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"hg", "[", "\"\<prop\>\"", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"1318f875-fdfb-f84e-850c-105d729ee7b1"],
 ". The available properties are given by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"hg", "[", "\"\<Properties\>\"", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d118be94-826d-b848-88e8-5d2b24d2b0b9"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fbc3006f-e23e-2044-a75b-bc332856b922"],

Cell["\<\
An invalid specification produces the message Hypergraph::spec and returns \
$Failed.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e28dd673-ebd6-2943-aa0a-01af201073c3"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"1751a1dc-e02b-2648-990e-21573706b1e8"],

Cell["From a list of edges; the vertex set is inferred:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"ca6151b5-75ad-a547-87e0-076d9cf01d84"],

